# Skillet backend — copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and uncomment only
# what you need. Every var below is OPTIONAL and commented out by default: a
# completely empty `.env` (or no `.env` at all — `make dev` copies this file
# for you on first run) still runs the full app in BYOK-only local mode — a
# learner supplies their own provider key per-request in the UI, and no
# trial/rate-limiting code activates without SKILLET_TRIAL_OPENAI_API_KEY set
# (see SPEC-distribution.md's Confirmed Decision 3 and
# SPEC-trial-limits.md's Confirmed Decision 11).
#
# Deliberately left COMMENTED OUT rather than `VAR=` (empty) below: several
# of these are read via `os.environ.get(KEY, default)`, which only falls
# back to `default` when the key is genuinely absent — an empty-but-present
# value (`VAR=`) is a *different*, falsy-but-not-missing value that some of
# these call sites do not special-case (verified empirically: an empty
# `SKILLET_CORS_ORIGINS=` line, uncommented, would silently allow zero CORS
# origins instead of falling back to the documented default). Uncomment a
# line and give it a real, non-empty value to actually change that setting.
#
# `uv run --env-file .env ...` (what `make dev`'s dev-backend target uses)
# loads this file's real `.env` counterpart automatically.

# --- CORS (recipe-framework / execution) ---

# Comma-separated list of origins the frontend is served from. Only needs
# uncommenting if the frontend runs somewhere other than the default dev
# port. Default when absent: http://localhost:3000
# SKILLET_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# --- trial-limits: keyless-trial gating (hosted-demo only) ---
#
# Leave this whole section commented out for a local/self-hosted clone.
# `gate_trial_run` treats an absent SKILLET_TRIAL_OPENAI_API_KEY as "no
# trial key funded" and short-circuits to pure BYOK for every request — a
# missing required key then fails with an ordinary 422, never a 429. Only
# the hosted demo (run by the project author) uncomments these.

# The author's own OpenAI key, used ONLY to cover a learner's first few
# trial runs on the hosted demo — never persisted, never logged (see
# scripts/check_trial_key_redaction.py). Leave commented out locally.
# SKILLET_TRIAL_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Upstash Redis REST credentials (https://upstash.com — free tier is
# enough), used for the per-device/IP trial counters. Required together
# with SKILLET_TRIAL_OPENAI_API_KEY above; leave both commented out locally.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-instance.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# HMAC secret used to sign the anonymous `sk_aid` trial-identity cookie.
# Required together with the two vars above. Generate a real one with:
# python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
# SKILLET_TRIAL_COOKIE_SECRET=...

# Max total spend (USD) the hosted demo allows across ALL trial users per
# UTC day, before every trial request is denied with a 429 regardless of any
# individual learner's own remaining quota (a global kill-switch).
# Default when absent: 5.00
# SKILLET_TRIAL_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=5.00

# Max number of trial runs a single device/IP may make per UTC day.
# Default when absent: 2
# SKILLET_TRIAL_DAILY_CAP=2
